---
title: Sloppy Joes
source: Matt
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
---

In a small bowl, mix together @worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1/2%tbsp}, @chili powder{1/4%tbsp}, @mustard{1/8%cups}, @ketchup{1/4%cups}, @tomato paste{4%oz}, @seasoned salt{1/2%tsp}, and @mild hot sauce{} to create a sauce.

In a #skillet{}, saute @onion{1/2} and @garlic{1%tbsp} in @butter{1%tbsp} until softened.

Add @ground beef{1%pound} and cook until browned, then drain the grease.

Mix in the sauce and serve.
